name vis-sun-1
timeout 200

# LOOKING INTO THE SUN -- the eye's own hard case, and the one damping term that is NOT a multiplier on
# the general daylight factor. doc/sensors.md §9.6b.
#
# The mechanism is different from dusk: intraocular scatter raises the BACKGROUND luminance, and
# contrast is measured against the background. Stiles-Holladay [T3] gives L_veil = 10*E/theta^2, and
# since neither the source illuminance nor the ambient luminance exists in absolute units in this tree,
# the whole relation collapses into ONE readable setting --
#
#     C_eff = C / (1 + k/theta_sun^2),   k = (10 deg)^2
#
# so the setting IS the off-sun angle at which contrast is halved. 45 deg -> 0.95, 30 -> 0.90,
# 10 -> 0.50, 5 -> 0.20, 2 -> 0.04, and inside 2 deg of the disc a hard cut: there the eye is not
# degraded, it is out of action.
#
# THE CONTROL IS vis-day.fbm's `trail`, AND THE GEOMETRY IS ITS VERBATIM COPY: a target 3 km ahead on
# the same heading, 100 kt slower, overtaken slowly enough that the 1 Hz look raster samples the closure
# every ~50 m. The ONE difference is where the sun stands. At 04:30Z on midsummer's day over the Broye
# it is at el 6.6 / az 62.6 -- low, and straight down the nose of an aircraft tracking 063, so the line
# of sight to the target runs within a few degrees of the disc. In vis-day.fbm the identical geometry is
# flown with the sun at el 65.8 / az 160.5, i.e. high and behind, and the glare factor is 0.99.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   telemetry    vis_glare -- the factor at the worst-placed contact, 1.0 = no glare
#   events.log   the `vis CONTACT` line and the `contrast` it carries; recompute the range from the pose
#                columns of the two telemetry files (this channel publishes no range, ever), and put it
#                beside vis-day.fbm's `trail` figure measured under the identical geometry
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the verdict AND the pass. A measurement rig, not a task.

time 2026-06-21T04:30:00Z

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.60000 6.90000 3000 63.0 300         # tracking 063 -- straight into the low sun
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 46.76313 7.36597 3000 300

unit dazzled
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.61103 6.93583 3000 63.0 200         # 3 km ahead ON the sun bearing, 100 kt slower
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  wp 46.76193 7.36686 3000 200
